law.text:
		The Board shall include in the Standards of Learning for health education for grade nine and grade 10 an in-person or online severe allergic reaction awareness training that includes the following content:

The definition of and distinction between normal allergic reaction and anaphylaxis;


Types of allergens, including common and less common allergens;


The signs and symptoms of normal allergic reaction and anaphylaxis;


Treatments for anaphylaxis; and


The proper response to suspected anaphylaxis, including notifying the nearest staff member trained to respond to anaphylaxis and administer epinephrine.
